    "problem": "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4}\\sqrt{x^{5}}dx.\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "Since $x\\ge0$ on the interval, $\\sqrt{x^5}=x^{5/2}$. Hence\n$$\\int_0^4\\sqrt{x^5}\\,dx=\\left[\\frac27x^{7/2}\\right]_0^4=\\frac27(128)=\\frac{256}{7}.$$",
